[h1]Additional Campaign Rules. Rusbar Edition[/h1]

[b]Version:[/b] 1.0.0
[b]For Crusader Kings III:[/b] 1.19.0.6
[b]Languages:[/b] English and Russian

Additional Campaign Rules provides campaign-start options for cultural traditions, truces, and finite council tasks. Standard behavior remains the default for every selectable rule.

[h2]Game Rules[/h2]

[list]
[*][b]Additional cultural traditions:[/b] default, +5, +10, +15, +45, or +95 slots for every culture.
[*][b]Cultural tradition cost:[/b] 100%, 75%, 50%, 25%, 10%, or free for cultures with a player-controlled culture head.
[*][b]Cultural reform cooldown:[/b] default, at most 25, 10, 5, or 1 year, or no cooldown for cultures with a player-controlled culture head.
[*][b]Truce duration:[/b] 100%, 75%, 50%, 25%, 10%, or 5% of the ordinary duration.
[*][b]Truce scope:[/b] all standard post-war truces, or only wars where a player was the primary attacker or primary defender. Participation only as an ally does not qualify.
[*][b]Finite council tasks:[/b] standard duration or no longer than 1 year, 6 months, 3 months, or 1 month. Acceleration applies only to councillors serving player-controlled rulers.
[/list]

[h2]Council Tasks[/h2]

Supported tasks are Integrate Title, Bestow Royal Favor, Increase Control, Develop County, Promote Culture, Convince De Jure, Find Secrets, Convert Faith in County, and Fabricate Claim.

Standard requirements, penalties, targets, events, outcomes, and side effects are preserved. Continuous tasks have no completion time and are intentionally outside this rule.

[h2]Global Manual Settings[/h2]

The CK3 engine does not expose several parameters to conditional game rules. They therefore apply campaign-wide, including to AI, and can be edited manually:

[list]
[*][b]common/defines/zzz_ACR_RE_culture_defines.txt[/b] — base cultural-reform progress, per-county slowdown, maximum duration, and tradition-replacement multiplier.
[*][b]common/defines/zzz_ACR_RE_lifestyle_defines.txt[/b] — adult lifestyle focus changes every 12 months instead of the standard 60.
[/list]

Both files include comments with the standard values. Exit the game completely before editing and change only the number to the right of “=”. A small personal patch loaded after ACR_RE is recommended for permanent custom values.

[h2]Technical Notes[/h2]

[list]
[*]Extra slots use hidden system innovations and are automatically applied to new hybrid and divergent cultures.
[*]Council acceleration is added after standard percentage penalties, preventing those penalties from consuming the selected boost.
[*]Council-task overrides are synchronized with Crusader Kings III 1.19.0.6.
[*]Mod-owned script objects use the ACR_RE_ prefix.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]

Mods changing the same cultural calculations, standard truce calculation, listed council tasks, or corresponding defines may require a compatibility patch. Finalize the rules before starting a new campaign whenever possible.

